  "scope": "Ordinary, leased and successor result-settlement routing moves to the product adapter. Native journals retain transaction/lease authority; local cache updates and visible group/successor discovery stay with the VM owner.",
  "limitations": [
    "Trusted composition after admission, not raw ingress or standalone generic VM completion authority. Caller and native journal validate context, leases and receipts.",
    "Publication can fail after the journal commits. The adapter neither retries hooks nor rolls back native side effects. Existing ephemeral and SQLite replay semantics remain distinct.",
    "Frozen coordinators retain shared journal, evaluator and group-visibility kernels. The tests establish routing compatibility, not independent implementations of those layers.",
    "Cancellation/retry settlement, group visibility, journal ownership, complete host-neutral durable recovery and physical extraction remain open; native maturity and completion stay unchanged.",
    "Local macOS Rust/SQLite verification only; no Linux, GUI or remote CI run, and no freshly exported standalone checkpoint."
  ],
